      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Okay, so now the devs have changed their mind about which state the setting should stay in, and I'm upvoting this because I actually want to prioritize friends first.\n\nThe reason is pretty similar - I go to raves a lot, but I usually have only a handful friends in there that I usually hang out with. I want their avatars to load first since I'm going to meet them first anyways, instead of wasting time loading a bunch of people who're just chatting at the spawn.\n\nHaving the option to prioritize friends is especially important if you connection to the VRC servers isn't very fast or stable. Friends are usually the people you'll interact first after entering a lobby, and you don't want to make them wait a minute or 2 before giving you hugs or headpats while you're stuck loading everyone else around you.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-03-18T01:08:27.680Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "At raves or similar events, a lot of users may have literally half of the instance on their friends list.\n\nIn these situations, we prioritize avatar downloads by distance to load the people we're talking to first. These settings help a lot! \"De-cluttering\" isn't enough reason to get rid of them.",
